==English==
{{wikipedia|''mea culpa''}}

===Etymology===
From the {{uder|en|la|-}} phrase {{m|la|meā culpā}} (“through my fault”), [[Appendix:Glossary#ablative case|ablative case]] of {{m|la|[[mea]] [[culpa]]|t=my fault, guilt}}, taken from the ''{{w|Confiteor}}'', a traditional penitential prayer in Western Christianity.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌmeɪ.əˈkʊl.pə/|/ˌmeɪ.əˈkʌl.pə/|/ˌmiː.əˈkʊl.pə/|/ˌmiː.əˈkʌl.pə/|nocount=1}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-mea culpa.wav|a=US}}

===Interjection===
{{head|en|interjection|nolinkhead=1}}

# My [[fault]], due to my [[error]]; I am to [[blame]].
#: {{syn|en|my bad|peccavi}}
#: {{coord|en|nostra culpa|tua culpa}} 

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|mea maxima culpa}}

====See also====
* {{l|en|I stand corrected}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|mea culpae|nolinkhead=1}}

# An instance of mea culpa; an [[apology]].
#: {{syn|en|peccavi}}
#: {{coord|en|nostra culpa|tua culpa}} 
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Ingenious and Diverting Letters of the Lady ⸺ Travels into Spain:{{nb...|Describing the Devotions, Nunneries, Humours, Customs, Laws, Militia, Trade, Diet, and Recreations of That People. Intermixt with Great Variety of Modern Adventures, and Surprising Accidents: Being the Truest and Best Remarks Extant on That Court and Country.}}|edition=2nd|location=London|publisher={{...|Printed for}} Samuel Crouch{{nb...|at the Corner of Pope’s-Head-Alley, next Cornhil}}|year=1692|page=62|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/ingeniousdiverti00aulniala/page/62/mode/1up|passage=For Example, when St. Anthony ſaid his Confiteor, which he did often enough, all the Spectators fell down on their Knees, and gave themſelves ſuch rude '''Mea Culpa’s''' as was enough to beat the breath out of their Bodies.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=January 13, 2018| work=Civil Beat |title=When There’s Nuke Headed Your Way, ‘Do What You Gotta Do’|author=Tad Bartimus|passage= Basketball had been replaced by breathless commentators cross-talking and speculating, politicians on split screens eagerly interrupting each other to find scapegoats, and most mute (male) state officials, including Hawaii Gov. David Ige, opening their mouths to sputter (paraphrasing here) — golly gee, we don’t know what happened, but we plan to find out — '''mea culpas'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Michael D. Shear; Jim Tankersley|title=Biden Defends Afghan Pullout and Declares an End to Nation-Building|work=The New York Times|date=2021-09-01|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/01/us/politics/biden-defends-afghanistan-withdrawal.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=The president refused to offer any sort of '''mea culpa''' on Tuesday, even as the Taliban celebrated their “independence” from America with gunfire in the streets of Kabul.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Simon Parkin|title=README.txt by Chelsea Manning review – secrets and spies|work=The Guardian|date=2022-10-27|url=https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/oct/27/readmetxt-by-chelsea-manning-review-secrets-and-spies|issn=0261-3077|passage=At her trial, lawyers convinced Manning to issue a '''mea culpa''': {{...}}}}

